{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way","id":1055378,"title":"Mage is biting us in the ass every step of the way","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-26T13:57:54-08:00","id":1055378,"title":"Mage is biting us in the ass every step of the way","content":"I've been running a mixed supernatural game now for about four weeks. Every session, at every turn it's the mages. Issue after issue. Perhaps the biggest that I'm not liking at all is the lack of resistance to spells for non mages. For instance, most Supers have some kind of resistance built into a power . Say for a vampire's Possession power it's :Intelligence+Intimidation+ Dominate \u2013 victim\u2019s Resolve&quot; And if it includes a super splat it applies across the board. so say it's - blood potency then it includes others like Wyrd. Part of the problem is that we are all learning the CoD rules together and I'm just not knowledgeable with the Mage rules enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:02:15-08:00","id":1055379,"title":"","content":"Well the obvious problem is you're trying to run a mixed game with a system that wasn't made for it. I get that they run off the same system, but they all have different themes to them, so when you put a mage in a mortal or vampire game it can be as drastic a change as starting a Mutants and Masterminds character alongside a group of Dungeons and Dragons characters and also a Call of Cthulhu investigator.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find balance between them because there wasn't any attempt to balance them.<br /> <br /> Also you seem to be starting learning a game by actually playing multiple different games, which can be a problem too and probably won't help the learning curve any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:39:53-08:00","id":1055419,"title":"","content":"One of the important things to know about Mage is that the game rarely questions whether or not an individual mage can or cannot do something (this is mostly built into the mage's gnosis and arcana ratings and/or praxis/rotes known). Rather, the game asks SHOULD or SHOULDN'T that mage do something. In fact, that distinction is a central theme to Mage the Awakening. <br /> <br /> That being said, if your mage players are casting offensive or reality distorting spells on sleepers they should be rolling for both paradox and wisdom loss. And if they make a habit of doing so, they will quickly find themselves laden with rapid wisdom loss and/or paradox conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:59:13-08:00","id":1055428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055419#post1055419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, if your mage players are casting offensive or reality distorting spells on sleepers they should be rolling for both paradox and wisdom loss. And if they make a habit of doing so, they will quickly find themselves laden with rapid wisdom loss and/or paradox conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is rather missing the point of the OP that Mage seems unbalanced compared to the other major splats. <br /> <br /> That said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4135_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4135\" data-vbnamecard=\"4135\">Blue Thomas</a> the closest anyone gets to being able to resist Mages are if a spell cast on them isn't calculated with enough Potency to overcome their Withstand. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> did an eloquent job of explaining why you're experiencing these problems with Mage in a mixed splat game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:05:29-08:00","id":1055432,"title":"","content":"It seems to me that paradox doesn't seem all that bad (at least for the moment. no one is over 2 gnosis) They are careful around sleepers, but supers they let the fur fly. Wasn't one of the main goals of the new rules were to make all splats playable with each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:11:48-08:00","id":1055434,"title":"","content":"God, no. It was to have them use the same rules so you could use them as Storyteller characters. The various game protagonists are anything but balanced against one another - mages, mummies, and demons are far more potent than anyone else, by design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:12:23-08:00","id":1055435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055432#post1055432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't one of the main goals of the new rules were to make all splats playable with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly.<br /> <br /> It'd be good if you provided some examples of issues you've had, maybe there are ways around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:13:17-08:00","id":1055436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055432#post1055432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that paradox doesn't seem all that bad (at least for the moment. no one is over 2 gnosis) They are careful around sleepers, but supers they let the fur fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Planning accordingly can help with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wasn't one of the main goals of the new rules were to make all splats playable with each other? </div> </div> </div>As in you can put a mage as an antagonist in a werewolf game, or go from playing a werewolf game to a vampire game without needing to get used to a drastically different rule set. Everyone uses the same Attribute + Skill rolls, for the most part, with variations of superpowers.<br /> <br /> Not for a werewolf, mage and Sin-Eater to be part of the same player group. It's <i>doable</i>, it's just increasingly complicated the more games you add and you have to make cuts when it comes to the various settings and possibly even mechanics.<br /> <br /> Technically the only game that's actually meant to be played with others, so far, as in everyone is on the same team is Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-26-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:15:19-08:00","id":1055438,"title":"","content":"Mage 2e was explicitly designed without reference to other lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:20:17-08:00","id":1055440,"title":"","content":"I think compatible, not playable. As in, the ST can bring in any elements from any other gameline and have no problem with conflicting rules. But I might be wrong. Either way Mage has a different power level compared to other splats and I would never advise using mages in a mixed group of player characters.<br /> \u200bEdit: What nofather and Axelgear said. Why do I type so slowly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:23:53-08:00","id":1055442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055432#post1055432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't one of the main goals of the new rules were to make all splats playable with each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The new rules&quot; (i.e. the 1e/nWoD rules) were made so that every gameline's characters were mechanically <i>compatible</i>. This is not and should not be mistaken for the same thing as having mechanical <i>parity</i>.<br /> <br /> Paradox is there primarily to steer character behavior toward methodical and prepared activity and make the stakes of oversight compound with experience \u2014 containing a Paradox is relatively easy and low-risk early on, but eventually you're likely to hit the point where risking a Paradox Condition is just more of a problem than having the chance that a spell goes sour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T16:53:51-08:00","id":1055451,"title":"","content":"If you want mages to play well with other splats you'll probably need to give said other splats a bit of bonus Experience, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:02:51-08:00","id":1055483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way#post1055378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been running a mixed supernatural game now for about four weeks. Every session, at every turn it's the mages. Issue after issue. Perhaps the biggest that I'm not liking at all is the lack of resistance to spells for non mages. For instance, most Supers have some kind of resistance built into a power . Say for a vampire's Possession power it's :Intelligence+Intimidation+ Dominate \u2013 victim\u2019s Resolve&quot; And if it includes a super splat it applies across the board. so say it's - blood potency then it includes others like Wyrd. Part of the problem is that we are all learning the CoD rules together and I'm just not knowledgeable with the Mage rules enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think you may have jumped the gun a bit on this endeavor, but that doesn't mean you won't succeed.<br /> <br /> My first world of darkness experience was ST'ing Mage (after playing as a PC in many D&amp;D games and hosting a couple of games of the Descent boardgame.)<br /> <br /> Mage, on its own, is hard to digest. I've read many threads stating that it can be one of the most demanding tabletop games just because of the sheer freedom that players enjoy. The task of digesting MULTIPLE rule-sets for splats is herculean to me. Mechanically, Vamps/Wolves/Mages enjoy all sorts of perks and weaknesses (as stated before, Paradox is its own system). They also have complex laws, communities, politics, social graces, goals, etc.<br /> <br /> I toyed with letting my players choose whatever splat they wanted and bought the Demon/Vamp/Wolf corebooks. I've perused through them to get a gist, but the material is pretty substantial. I decided against it because I didn't want to make declarations that would later be revealed to be nonsensical, contradictory, or just plain ignorant.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I sometimes wish I started with Hunter or Vamp, to get used to the systems and rudimentary rolls without having to juggle wanton creativity and OP mage shenanigans. I could also severely curtail active times (sunlight being a huge obstacle for Vamps), and with either Hunter or Vamp I could craft pretty straight forward villains that don't run the gambit of being too prepared or under prepared.<br /> <br /> I assume it is too late to fall back into a single splat since characters have already been created.<br /> <br /> I think you can make it work, but you'll basically end up studying all the material like you have a midterm on it. The biggest help for me was Reddit and these forums. You get immersed in the methodology of playing and running these games. So look up keywords associated with whatever issues you're running into and consume. Pay special attention to disagreements about mechanics, as they often reveal how or why something was designed a certain way. People are usually pretty good with supplying simplified analogies for confusing concepts, too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:10:46-08:00","id":1055486,"title":"","content":"A common houserule was to have supernaturals add their Supernatural Tolerance trait (Blood Potency, Primal Urge, etc) to their Withstand ratings.<br /> <br /> Or use the higher of the two traits, if straight adding it reverses the tables and make the mages impotent at affecting non-humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:48:54-08:00","id":1055497,"title":"","content":"Changelings with high clarity can add their clarity to the their withstand rating when spending willpower I think according to 2e Changeling play test. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if this was the primary reason that was added to clarity, so Mages could just run rough shod over Changelings. <br /> <br /> I have to be honest, I bough Mage more for the insights into the WoD cosmology, then to actually play it, because I find Mages rules extremely complex compared to other splats, its the least beginner friendly of the games along with Mummy.<br /> <br /> Both have great flavour however.<br /> <br /> But if your new to CoD you should go with Mortals, Paranormal Mortals, Vampires, Werewolves (I'm guessing), Changelings, Beasts, and maybe Demons (I'm not complete certain about demon, but from what I've heard to rules are likely more easily grasped then Mage or Mummy).<br /> <br /> If I wanted to use the Mage or Mummy settings I'd use their near Mortal Splats instead, like Proximi. Simpler, infact they're likely perfect training wheels for mage and mummy games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:53:35-08:00","id":1055499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055486#post1055486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A common houserule was to have supernaturals add their Supernatural Tolerance trait (Blood Potency, Primal Urge, etc) to their Withstand ratings.<br /> <br /> Or use the higher of the two traits, if straight adding it reverses the tables and make the mages impotent at affecting non-humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWe use the higher of either traits with the caveat that exceptional success blows right through any supernatural tolerance or withstand rating. If we're doing crossover. Straight mage doesn't apply to said houserule and ONLY counts for PC non-mage supernatural types in crossover regardless. This isn't the Justice League/Superfriends here. You can be a special snowflake and play another supernatural with a cabal of mages but it still isn't going to be completely even because mages like a couple other supernatural types are supposed to be more powerful then the others by intention. Mages are supposed to be assholes that bend reality just because they can. And that includes other supernatural types when dealt with on an individual basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-26-2017, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:22:40-08:00","id":1055894,"title":"","content":"I had a similar question because I realized that Mages do have tremendous powers over other supernatural characters. There was a thread which stated that a mage could possess a group of other supernaturals using psychic domination. I thought it was a mistake, but then I realized that with rotes such a thing is possible. Here is my logic, and please correct me if I am wrong or missed something.<br /> <br /> A beginner mage runs into a pack of werewolves, or a coterie of vampires, a group of hunters...<br /> <br /> The mage is just starting off and has Gnosis 1 and Mind 3, giving him a pool of 4 dice. However, he does have a rote in psychic domination. Lets just say that his skill is 4 plus he has a magical tool giving him another dice, so he gets 5 bonus dice for having his Yantas, the maximum. So he has 9 dice. He will try to dominate the group and assumes he must overcome 3 resolve to get most of them so he subtracts 6 dice to get 3 Potency. He can still roll 3 dice which is still a pretty good chance of success.<br /> <br /> Next is reach, since it is a rote he gets 4 free reach. <br /> He spends 2 to get the group to do anything he wants as per the spell<br /> he spends 1 to get the spell instant rather than have to wait 3 hours<br /> he spends 1 to cast at sensory range<br /> he spends 1 to affect 5 people, rather than 1<br /> he spends 1 to extend duration to a scene<br /> <br /> Since this is 6, he gets 2 paradox dice, not a great danger I am guessing considering the size of the feat he is doing.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe that someone can blow willpower which would add 2 to the resistance trait and thereby scuttle the spell which makes sense, but the potential for this powerful spell is really great. Please let me know if I missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:38:11-08:00","id":1055905,"title":"","content":"Seems right. You would likely take a Wisdom hit or two but you could get a Legacy or inure yourself and be set. I often point out that it's fortunate that people don't get experience based on the numbers of NPCs slain in these games. But without knowing the game well, it's easy to see a Storyteller not planning quite accordingly. And, of course, in a multi-game group of players you are going to get situations like D&amp;D's wizard and sorcerer being objectively better than everyone else, though that relies a lot on white room theorizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:52:39-08:00","id":1055914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055894#post1055894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage is just starting off and has Gnosis 1 and Mind 3, giving him a pool of 4 dice. However, he does have a rote in psychic domination. Lets just say that his skill is 4 plus he has a magical tool giving him another dice, so he gets 5 bonus dice for having his Yantas, the maximum. So he has 9 dice. He will try to dominate the group and assumes he must overcome 3 resolve to get most of them so he subtracts 6 dice to get 3 Potency. He can still roll 3 dice which is still a pretty good chance of success.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe that someone can blow willpower which would add 2 to the resistance trait and thereby scuttle the spell which makes sense, but the potential for this powerful spell is really great. Please let me know if I missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonuses from Yantra are used primarily to offset dice penalties, they cap out at +5 after that, a Mage could use more to gain greater factors before capping out.<br /> <br /> Also, that +2 to their Resistance trait from expending WP lasts a turn, after which the spell would take effect as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:28:55-08:00","id":1055982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055894#post1055894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a similar question because I realized that Mages do have tremendous powers over other supernatural characters. There was a thread which stated that a mage could possess a group of other supernaturals using psychic domination. I thought it was a mistake, but then I realized that with rotes such a thing is possible. Here is my logic, and please correct me if I am wrong or missed something.<br /> <br /> A beginner mage runs into a pack of werewolves, or a coterie of vampires, a group of hunters...<br /> <br /> The mage is just starting off and has Gnosis 1 and Mind 3, giving him a pool of 4 dice. However, he does have a rote in psychic domination. Lets just say that his skill is 4 plus he has a magical tool giving him another dice, so he gets 5 bonus dice for having his Yantas, the maximum. So he has 9 dice. He will try to dominate the group and assumes he must overcome 3 resolve to get most of them so he subtracts 6 dice to get 3 Potency. He can still roll 3 dice which is still a pretty good chance of success.<br /> <br /> Next is reach, since it is a rote he gets 4 free reach.<br /> He spends 2 to get the group to do anything he wants as per the spell<br /> he spends 1 to get the spell instant rather than have to wait 3 hours<br /> he spends 1 to cast at sensory range<br /> he spends 1 to affect 5 people, rather than 1<br /> he spends 1 to extend duration to a scene<br /> <br /> Since this is 6, he gets 2 paradox dice, not a great danger I am guessing considering the size of the feat he is doing.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe that someone can blow willpower which would add 2 to the resistance trait and thereby scuttle the spell which makes sense, but the potential for this powerful spell is really great. Please let me know if I missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks fine except additional yantra's past the first require an extra turn. So using 2 is 2 turns casting...which might cause problems if grappled/mauled in the mean time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:37:52-08:00","id":1055985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055914#post1055914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, that +2 to their Resistance trait from expending WP lasts a turn, after which the spell would take effect as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait is this right? Say somebody has enough normal resistance trait to withstand a spell with x duration and then somebody else comes along in the meantime and lowers his resistance trait i assume the spell wont suddenly take effect? Its taken effect on others who didnt withstand it but the spell itself has been cast you avoided its effects when they were created, the spell effects wont suddenly turn on later.<br /> <br /> If you withstand a spell it washes over you with no effect, you dont keep rechecking to see if it applies right? Maybe if the spell was an area effect spell but even then id say you would be fine even if your resistant trait dropped lower than the spells potency and would only reaffirm itself if you left and reentered the area of effect. Is that right? Im not sure.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T22:22:24-08:00","id":1055995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055985#post1055985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait is this right? Say somebody has enough normal resistance trait to withstand a spell with x duration and then somebody else comes along in the meantime and lowers his resistance trait i assume the spell wont suddenly take effect? Its taken effect on others who didnt withstand it but the spell itself has been cast you avoided its effects when they were created, the spell effects wont suddenly turn on later.<br /> <br /> If you withstand a spell it washes over you with no effect, you dont keep rechecking to see if it applies right? Maybe if the spell was an area effect spell but even then id say you would be fine even if your resistant trait dropped lower than the spells potency and would only reaffirm itself if you left and reentered the area of effect. Is that right? Im not sure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If the spell has a duration longer than one turn it remains on the target until that duration is up, regardless of whether they Withstand it or not. If someone lowers their Resistance trait to below being able to Withstand the spell the spell then takes effect. Now, I think that If they know that this is happening and are able and willing to spend a point of Willpower they can add +2 to their Withstand for (I think) 1 turn, potentially allowing themselves to act without being affected by said spell for that 1 turn (or as long as they are still able and willing to spend Willpower).<br /> <br /> Edit: So yeah, as long as a spell remains in effect it does constantly recheck to see if it applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 02-28-2017, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:31:35-08:00","id":1056021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055995#post1055995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the spell has a duration longer than one turn it remains on the target until that duration is up, regardless of whether they Withstand it or not. If someone lowers their Resistance trait to below being able to Withstand the spell the spell then takes effect. Now, I think that If they know that this is happening and are able and willing to spend a point of Willpower they can add +2 to their Withstand for (I think) 1 turn, potentially allowing themselves to act without being affected by said spell for that 1 turn (or as long as they are still able and willing to spend Willpower).<br /> <br /> Edit: So yeah, as long as a spell remains in effect it does constantly recheck to see if it applies.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If this leaves the spell with no<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> levels in Potency, it still counts as an active spell against spell<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> control but has no further effect.</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>If a person withstands a spell the spell has no further effect. just because the trait changes later doesnt make a blind bit of difference as i see it. There is no written examples of it continually checking its status. It says quite clearly that spell that you withstood even if others havent has no further effect on you but still counts as a active spell for the mage who cast it during its duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-28-2017, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T02:55:36-08:00","id":1056030,"title":"","content":"You cite it yourself. If the spell has no levels in Potency left, it has no effect. When the spell is still active and your withstandrating lowers, it HAS levels in potency left afterwards and therefore takes effect. This question has been discussed on this board and what everybody is telling you is the conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:55:58-08:00","id":1056045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056021#post1056021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a person withstands a spell the spell has no further effect. just because the trait changes later doesnt make a blind bit of difference as i see it. There is no written examples of it continually checking its status. It says quite clearly that spell that you withstood even if others havent has no further effect on you but still counts as a active spell for the mage who cast it during its duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>The spell is still active as you noted it takes up spell control still, the text you quote doesn't discuss what happens when Withstand is lowered after the spell is Withstood. The Potency put into the spell doesn't change so if Withstand goes under Potency the spell comes online with the reduced Potency effect that Withstand grants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:11:54-08:00","id":1056080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056045#post1056045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The spell is still active as you noted it takes up spell control still, the text you quote doesn't discuss what happens when Withstand is lowered after the spell is Withstood. The Potency put into the spell doesn't change so if Withstand goes under Potency the spell comes online with the reduced Potency effect that Withstand grants.</div> </div> </div> </div>hmm, not convinced, surely it would state this in the text somewhere? Withstand is checked when the spell is cast and that's it, if it was checked constantly then surely the text would state it as such with something along the lines of &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">it still counts as an active spell against spell<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> control but has no further effect <b>until the withstand is lower than its potency.&quot;</b> Seems like alot of extra book keeping otherwise, i cast spell with potency 6 on somebody with withstand 4 then later choose to lower its potency by 2 and now the spell switches off? Or i cast spells on people with potency 2 vs somebody with a withstand of 4 but get my friend to lower his withstand stat</span></span></span></span></span></span> to one and suddenly my spell springs back into life?<br /> <br /> Another example: I cross the gauntlet in the forest which is withstood with the gauntlet strength, my potency is 3 and the gauntlet rating is 2 from being in the wilderness, the spell doesnt end when i move into the city does it? The withstand rating is now 4 as soon as i get into the city suburbs and all of a sudden my spell stops working? I dont think so.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-28-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:15:12-08:00","id":1056083,"title":"","content":"Withstand <i>eats</i> potency. You don't get it back no matter what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:26:43-08:00","id":1056085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056080#post1056080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or i cast spells on people with potency 2 vs somebody with a withstand of 4 but get my friend to lower his withstand stat to one and suddenly my spell springs back into life?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the intention as I understand it, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:40:37-08:00","id":1056245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056080#post1056080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another example: I cross the gauntlet in the forest which is withstood with the gauntlet strength, my potency is 3 and the gauntlet rating is 2 from being in the wilderness, the spell doesnt end when i move into the city does it? The withstand rating is now 4 as soon as i get into the city suburbs and all of a sudden my spell stops working? I dont think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossing the Gauntlet works differently. Notice that the &quot;World Walker&quot; spell has Potency as its Primary Factor. It's not Duration, because the spell only lasts long enough to place you in the Spirit World. Once you're there, the spell had ended, and you can stay there indefinitely. The &quot;Reaching&quot; spell also allows you to cross the Gauntlet, as long as you spend Reach to create an Iris. True, &quot;Reaching&quot; has Duration as its Primary Factor, but that refers to its basic effect, which lets you act across the Gauntlet without crossing it. If you cast that lesser version, moving to the city DOES prevent you from interacting with the Spirit World, until you return to the forest or cast a stronger spell. It's like losing cellphone reception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:47:47-08:00","id":1056249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056245#post1056245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossing the Gauntlet works differently. Notice that the &amp;quot;World Walker&amp;quot; spell has Potency as its Primary Factor. It's not Duration, because the spell only lasts long enough to place you in the Spirit World. Once you're there, the spell had ended, and you can stay there indefinitely. The &amp;quot;Reaching&amp;quot; spell also allows you to cross the Gauntlet, as long as you spend Reach to create an Iris. True, &amp;quot;Reaching&amp;quot; has Duration as its Primary Factor, but that refers to its basic effect, which lets you act across the Gauntlet without crossing it. If you cast that lesser version, moving to the city DOES prevent you from interacting with the Spirit World, until you return to the forest or cast a stronger spell. It's like losing cellphone reception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I was pretty skeptical of the interpretation that a filly Withstood spell takes effect if the subject's Withstand drops low enough during its Duration, but this post has about convinced me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:12:32-08:00","id":1056262,"title":"","content":"In the mass mind control one, you'd want to shift up, to become immune via size since the size of the largest target is still 5. Though it's entirely possible to just have more than 3 Resolve and be immune that way.<br /> <br /> While I understand Withstand and why it's done the way it is, instead of using Power Stat, it seems weird that it inverses for ephemerals, and uses Rank, which is effectively their Power Stat. Again, I get why, but with the difference like that it's just more obvious that the smaller number was picked to make it easier to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-28-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:19:38-08:00","id":1056267,"title":"","content":"I'm curious does a mage know if they're spell was whitstood? If they are the I can't imagine a mage continuing to invest spell control to keep it going and doing nothing. Also I'm pretty sure that a comment elfive made a out it &quot;eating&quot; potency is correct. The spells potency is permanently lowered after it faces off with a targets whitstand. As far as I know they're still no way to increase a spells potency after its cast which means if a spell is left with 0 potency it's dead in the water in most cases","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:25:50-08:00","id":1056272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056267#post1056267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious does a mage know if they're spell was whitstood?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem like it, though I've only glanced through the first Withstanding sections to check. In some cases it should be obvious, the target not shrinking, for instance. I'd say no, but I expect some Storytellers would be more lenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are the I can't imagine a mage continuing to invest spell control to keep it going and doing nothing. Also I'm pretty sure that a comment elfive made a out it &quot;eating&quot; potency is correct. The spells potency is permanently lowered after it faces off with a targets whitstand. As far as I know they're still no way to increase a spells potency after its cast which means if a spell is left with 0 potency it's dead in the water in most cases </div> </div> </div>Yeah. 'Withstood spells reduce their Potency by levels equal to the Withstand rating. If this leaves the spell with no levels in Potency, it still counts as an active spell against spell control but has no further effect.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:26:21-08:00","id":1056273,"title":"","content":"I would suspect they do since they would notice it did not have the intended effect. I am not sure if Potency is eaten, since Potency really is not a factor so long as there is at least 1 Potency for the spell to take effect. I imagine the spell would sit with its Potency in tact but not doing anything, plus a Potency 0 spell would not exist since that is the same as a failed cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:37:27-08:00","id":1056279,"title":"","content":"I did a little more digging. It seems like no unless a spell effect is obvious a mage doesn't inherently know if it was whitstood. However they could take a peak with mage sight to determine its potency.(not so useful in the middle of a heated exchange of course).<br /> <br /> As for eating potency I was referencing an earlier line of comments on this thread where it was suggested that if somehow someone's whitstood trait was lowered they could be effected by the spell afterwards. I'm pretty sure that's not true because the spells potency has been lowered to 0. If it wasn't lowered to 0 it still works as you said taldor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:54:28-08:00","id":1056287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did a little more digging. It seems like no unless a spell effect is obvious a mage doesn't inherently know if it was whitstood. However they could take a peak with mage sight to determine its potency.(not so useful in the middle of a heated exchange of course). </div> </div> </div>I did wonder about subtle effects, thanks for finding this! Know to be tricky to my players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:08:06-08:00","id":1056290,"title":"","content":"About 'eating Potency', its RAW that a spell that targets multiple Targets is Withstood seperatley for each, but would be Dispelled as a single spell, so the Potency of a spell itself is not reduced if one target Withstands it, it just doesn't affect that Target. I think it is logical that if the Target that did Withstand were to have a change in their Withstand rating then the spell could start to affect that target as well as any others. And then there is no reason not have that sam e apply to s single Target spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:30:36-08:00","id":1056300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056290#post1056290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About 'eating Potency', its RAW that a spell that targets multiple Targets is Withstood seperatley for each, but would be Dispelled as a single spell, so the Potency of a spell itself is not reduced if one target Withstands it, it just doesn't affect that Target. I think it is logical that if the Target that did Withstand were to have a change in their Withstand rating then the spell could start to affect that target as well as any others. And then there is no reason not have that sam e apply to s single Target spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the way I understand it too. Potency is not lost, the spell just does not have any effect. Also, it still is effected by Spell Control, which to me means it still has a Potency, because a Potency 0 spell in my mind would not register under spell control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:38:47-08:00","id":1056370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056290#post1056290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About 'eating Potency', its RAW that a spell that targets multiple Targets is Withstood seperatley for each, but would be Dispelled as a single spell, so the Potency of a spell itself is not reduced if one target Withstands it, it just doesn't affect that Target. I think it is logical that if the Target that did Withstand were to have a change in their Withstand rating then the spell could start to affect that target as well as any others. And then there is no reason not have that sam e apply to s single Target spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure for spells with multiple targets, each target treats the spell as having its Potency lowered by their Withstand value. So, it might be reduced to 0 for one target, meaning it has no effect on them, but be only partially reduced for another target, still taking effect, but to a lesser degree than it would have if it was not Withstood. The question is, if said spell has a Duration longer than an instantaneous one-off effect, and one or more of the targets have their Withstand trait increased or decreased during that time, does the spell's Potency increase or decrease for that (or those) target (or targets) accordingly?<br /> <br /> For example, lets say I cast a spell on a group of five people that penalizes the target's attack dice pools by Potency for the Duration. Lets say that I set the Potency to 4 and the Duration to 1 scene. Lets say that this spell is Withstood by Composure. If in the five people affected, three have Composure 2 and two have Composure 3, two will have a -1 penalty to attack rolls for the Scenr and three will have a -2 penalty. If one of the people with Composure 3 somehow gains a dot of Composure during the scene, does it stop affecting him? If one of the people with Composure 2 loses a dot of Composure during the scene, does her penalty Increase to -3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T17:28:50-08:00","id":1056388,"title":"","content":"In the mind control example, I think I have been able to resolve it somewhat in my mind.<br /> <br /> Compare a starting Vampire with Dominate 2 trying to do the same thing, the vampire can look into the eyes of another supernatural and roll a larger dice pool than his opponent since he has 3 traits rather than one plus a supernatural trait, so lets say 8 dice is resisted by 5 dice and the vampire can reasonably control someone by looking in his eyes. He gets all the stuff that the Mage was trying to do with reach only he gets it automatically. The only thing he does not get is the ability to control multiple targets but all other factors are taken care of more or less. Also recall that I am using a buffed up mind control mage which buffed up his mind control power which is something of an outlier anyways. Sometimes I feel that Mages must fight for things that other supernaturals get automatically. Even a mage who wakes up early in the morning to perform a 15 hour ritual to buff his strength to 9 will probably still get mauled by a werewolf or vampire since he would not have the other bells and whistles such as regeneration, speed, claws etc...<br /> <br /> Another thing is that I recall that some powers such as gifts and promethean powers are designed to withstand mental influence which would cause a clash of wills, and to give a power like this a counterweight.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the said mage would probably be best doing this spell early in his career since later on, as his gnosis goes up, the paradox from so much Reach could probably cause the spell to (literally), blow up in his face.<br /> <br /> Also, a mage in an alley way would need to use 2 Yantras which would take at least 2 turns, and each subsequent attempt would as well only with more paradox. During this time the werewolf pack would see someone waving a magic wand at them and uttering some strange language. They would feel someone trying to mess with their mind which they would, naturally, try to resist. The situation would probably escalate quite quickly in which the werewolves would probably react in a spectacularly brutal fashion, ending the mage right then and there.<br /> <br /> Finally, as great as crossovers are, the World of Darkness is a busy place. All the supernaturals are so busy with their agendas (doing politics, fighting spirits, opposing Seers...), that they cannot bother with each other. A mage's main antagonist will probably be another mage such as a Seer who has lots of ways to counter his magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1107,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","user":"maryshelly","date":". 02-28-2017, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:32:58-08:00","id":1056407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056370#post1056370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, lets say I cast a spell on a group of five people that penalizes the target's attack dice pools by Potency for the Duration. Lets say that I set the Potency to 4 and the Duration to 1 scene. Lets say that this spell is Withstood by Composure. If in the five people affected, three have Composure 2 and two have Composure 3, two will have a -1 penalty to attack rolls for the Scenr and three will have a -2 penalty. If one of the people with Composure 3 somehow gains a dot of Composure during the scene, does it stop affecting him? If one of the people with Composure 2 loses a dot of Composure during the scene, does her penalty Increase to -3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been saying that since you check for withstand only when the spell is cast and potency for everybody is set at that time, changes to a withstand rating after a spell affects you or not wont matter, the spell doesn't reaffirm itself on you if your withstand lowers. Others seem to think spells reaffirm themselves if your withstand rating lowers to below its original potency, im not sure why because there is no text that can find that supports this view. Seems like if it worked like this, there would be some explanation since its a pretty complex system if you have to take note of potency when the spell is cast and check it again if withstand rating changes later etc. For me the &quot;no further effect&quot; means just that even if the spell is still technically around it just has zero potency vs you and wont be getting it back just because your withstand rating has changed since the spell was cast.<br /> <br /> Not sure the etiquette of pm'ing Dave for an answer or why this hasnt come up before. Somebody did mention it had been discussed before but didnt link the thread, i had searched before hand and couldnt find a conclusive answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 02-28-2017, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:02:03-08:00","id":1056417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056407#post1056407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been saying that since you check for withstand only when the spell is cast and potency for everybody is set at that time, changes to a withstand rating after a spell affects you or not wont matter, the spell doesn't reaffirm itself on you if your withstand lowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly the easiest way to handle it, bookkeeping-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056407#post1056407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Others seem to think spells reaffirm themselves if your withstand rating lowers to below its original potency,</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not saying that the spell <i>reaffirms</i> itself. They're saying that the spell hangs around during its full duration, and that anyone whose Withstand is low enough is affected by it, regardless of when or how their Withstand happened to be too low. It's like standing in a cloud of tear gas while wearing a gas mask. The gas mask doesn't prevent the gas from permeating the area after it's first released, and it doesn't stop you from being affected if someone pulls the mask off.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that both interpretations are valid, though I tend to lean toward easy bookkeeping for practical reasons.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... In a related issue, would a spell that had an area of effect (rather than discrete targets) affect people as they entered the area, or would it only affect everyone in the area at the time of casting? In both cases, the spell would have a duration--either maintaining an effect on the unlucky few, or remaining as the aforementioned cloud of gas, indiscriminately hurting all comers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:34:28-08:00","id":1056420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056417#post1056417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... In a related issue, would a spell that had an area of effect (rather than discrete targets) affect people as they entered the area, or would it only affect everyone in the area at the time of casting? In both cases, the spell would have a duration--either maintaining an effect on the unlucky few, or remaining as the aforementioned cloud of gas, indiscriminately hurting all comers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is absolutely the former as shown by Space 4's Alter Direction. As long as the spell is in effect it takes hold of anything and everything in the area, regardless of whether said person or object was in the area at the time the spell was originally cast or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:47:17-08:00","id":1056423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056420#post1056420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is absolutely the former as shown by Space 4's Alter Direction. As long as the spell is in effect it takes hold of anything and everything in the area, regardless of whether said person or object was in the area at the time the spell was originally cast or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it depends on how you cast the spell. When you're deciding scale you have to choose between Number of Subjects and Area of Effect.<br /> <br /> 'If the mage uses Number of Subjects for Scale, the factor determines how many subjects may be affected and the Size of the largest subject. Once decided, a mage can affect fewer subjects than the scale of her spell permits. <br /> If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within.'<br /> <br /> With the former, it seems like your spell would cling to those people targeted and only those people, this is bad if a new person shows up. With the latter, it would only affect the area, which is bad if they leave the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T19:50:32-08:00","id":1056426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056423#post1056423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it depends on how you cast the spell. When you're deciding scale you have to choose between Number of Subjects and Area of Effect.<br /> <br /> 'If the mage uses Number of Subjects for Scale, the factor determines how many subjects may be affected and the Size of the largest subject. Once decided, a mage can affect fewer subjects than the scale of her spell permits.<br /> If using Area of Effect for Scale, the factor instead determines how large the area covered by the spell is, applying the spell effect to anyone or anything within.'<br /> <br /> With the former, it seems like your spell would cling to those people targeted and only those people, this is bad if a new person shows up. With the latter, it would only affect the area, which is bad if they leave the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunatus specifically asked about spells cast with an area of effect, so the other side of Scale isn't really relevant here. If cast on an area, anything and everything in the area is affected as long as the spell remains active, regardless of if they were in the area as it was cast or if they just happened to walk in a bit later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:11:22-08:00","id":1056439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056426#post1056426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunatus specifically asked about spells cast with an area of effect, so the other side of Scale isn't really relevant here.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056426#post1056426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If cast on an area, anything and everything in the area is affected as long as the spell remains active, regardless of if they were in the area as it was cast or if they just happened to walk in a bit later.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, if I cast a spell that causes a gout of flame to rush through a large house, not knowing how many people are in said house, and therefore not using Scale to affect a discrete number of people, but using Duration to make sure that those affected burn for the next few rounds, I <i>must</i> have that gout of flame remain raging throughout the entire house? It seems to me that the imago of the spell also comes into play here. (Perhaps I'm reading more into your post than was intended. My apologies if that's so.)<br /> <br /> That said, Alter Direction is an excellent point. Area of effect spells clearly have the option of being a persistent effect field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:38:51-08:00","id":1056450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056439#post1056439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, if I cast a spell that causes a gout of flame to rush through a large house, not knowing how many people are in said house, and therefore not using Scale to affect a discrete number of people, but using Duration to make sure that those affected burn for the next few rounds, I <i>must</i> have that gout of flame remain raging throughout the entire house? It seems to me that the imago of the spell also comes into play here. (Perhaps I'm reading more into your post than was intended. My apologies if that's so.)<br /> <br /> That said, Alter Direction is an excellent point. Area of effect spells clearly have the option of being a persistent effect field.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much. Area of Effect is pretty damn indiscriminate. Hell, if you were in the house yourself and cast such a spell you'd set yourself on fire too. AoE use of Scale in a spell hits all valid targets, regardless of anything else. The only real exception is if you use Fate 2's Warding Gesture, which is pretty much the only thing that would let you exclude friendlies and or innocents from your AoEs (assuming you tag them with it before hand).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:46:32-08:00","id":1056477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056450#post1056450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, pretty much. Area of Effect is pretty damn indiscriminate. Hell, if you were in the house yourself and cast such a spell you'd set yourself on fire too. AoE use of Scale in a spell hits all valid targets, regardless of anything else. The only real exception is if you use Fate 2's Warding Gesture, which is pretty much the only thing that would let you exclude friendlies and or innocents from your AoEs (assuming you tag them with it before hand).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo conjunctional spells aren't a thing anymore? A Forces 3+/Fate 2 spell should be simple if you prefer not to use targeting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:10:32-08:00","id":1056485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056477#post1056477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSo conjunctional spells aren't a thing anymore? A Forces 3+/Fate 2 spell should be simple if you prefer not to use targeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, there is only 1 mention of &quot;conjuctional&quot; in the entire book most spells now will now tell you what addition arcana you can add to do another effect and the conjuctional name has been dropped. There are also now attainments that can alter the way spells work, like sympathy and conditional duration, to exclude people from spells you now need to use a fate 2 spell called Warding Gesture.<br /> <br /> Ok, hmm, Say i cast a spell that turns everybody in an area into a frog. There is currently 3 people in the area. A,B and C, my spell works on A &amp; B but C has a higher withstand and so the spell faiils on them. A &amp; B are frogs, they will continue to be frogs until the spells duration ends even if they leave the area of effect right because my spell is making them a frog. Anybody else entering the area of effect will or wont be turned into a frog? I think that the spell will get cast agan every Gnosis limit if it also has a duration longer than instant and anybody in the area at that time will get turned into frogs? Thats how i see it working. If people do get turned into frogs by entering the area any time during its duration then C is still immune right (and i believe even if its withstand rating has changed) still its still the same spell?<br /> <br /> If you cast a aoe healing spell with a duration longer than instant, it will heal everybody in the area once and again every gnosis level? This is how i see every one time effect aoe spell working..<br /> <br /> Obv aoe spells that are creating/manipulating in their aoe will work differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:19:16-08:00","id":1056488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1055894#post1055894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a similar question because I realized that Mages do have tremendous powers over other supernatural characters. There was a thread which stated that a mage could possess a group of other supernaturals using psychic domination. I thought it was a mistake, but then I realized that with rotes such a thing is possible. Here is my logic, and please correct me if I am wrong or missed something.<br /> <br /> A beginner mage runs into a pack of werewolves, or a coterie of vampires, a group of hunters...<br /> <br /> The mage is just starting off and has Gnosis 1 and Mind 3, giving him a pool of 4 dice. However, he does have a rote in psychic domination. Lets just say that his skill is 4 plus he has a magical tool giving him another dice, so he gets 5 bonus dice for having his Yantas, the maximum. So he has 9 dice. He will try to dominate the group and assumes he must overcome 3 resolve to get most of them so he subtracts 6 dice to get 3 Potency. He can still roll 3 dice which is still a pretty good chance of success.<br /> <br /> Next is reach, since it is a rote he gets 4 free reach.<br /> He spends 2 to get the group to do anything he wants as per the spell<br /> he spends 1 to get the spell instant rather than have to wait 3 hours<br /> he spends 1 to cast at sensory range<br /> he spends 1 to affect 5 people, rather than 1<br /> he spends 1 to extend duration to a scene<br /> <br /> Since this is 6, he gets 2 paradox dice, not a great danger I am guessing considering the size of the feat he is doing.<br /> <br /> Now, I believe that someone can blow willpower which would add 2 to the resistance trait and thereby scuttle the spell which makes sense, but the potential for this powerful spell is really great. Please let me know if I missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty spot on and why rotes are valued and just think about it when the creator of said rote gets rote action on top. And adds exceptional success to the mix as easily as breathing. Masters don't have to show off unless they have a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:31:21-08:00","id":1056491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056485#post1056485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of, there is only 1 mention of &quot;conjuctional&quot; in the entire book most spells now will now tell you what addition arcana you can add to do another effect and the conjuctional name has been dropped. There are also now attainments that can alter the way spells work, like sympathy and conditional duration, to exclude people from spells you now need to use a fate 2 spell called Warding Gesture.<br /> <br /> Ok, hmm, Say i cast a spell that turns everybody in an area into a frog. There is currently 3 people in the area. A,B and C, my spell works on A &amp; B but C has a higher withstand and so the spell faiils on them. A &amp; B are frogs, they will continue to be frogs until the spells duration ends even if they leave the area of effect right because my spell is making them a frog. Anybody else entering the area of effect will or wont be turned into a frog? I think that the spell will get cast agan every Gnosis limit if it also has a duration longer than instant and anybody in the area at that time will get turned into frogs? Thats how i see it working. If people do get turned into frogs by entering the area any time during its duration then C is still immune right (and i believe even if its withstand rating has changed) still its still the same spell?<br /> <br /> If you cast a aoe healing spell with a duration longer than instant, it will heal everybody in the area once and again every gnosis level? This is how i see every one time effect aoe spell working..<br /> <br /> Obv aoe spells that are creating/manipulating in their aoe will work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bInteresting it's similar to Mage the Ascension but less harsh. You get your two favored Arcanum then get a third by legacy and make sure Fate/Space/Time are at two dots. To do the sculpted AOE spells/sympathy and the contingency type spells or triggered effects. Similar but easier. And it's damn useful to have three Arcanum at 5 dots and only have to get 2-3 dots in 2 maybe three others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:46:48-08:00","id":1056493,"title":"","content":"Combined spells are still a thing right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:05:54-08:00","id":1056497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056439#post1056439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if I cast a spell that causes a gout of flame to rush through a large house, not knowing how many people are in said house, and therefore not using Scale to affect a discrete number of people, but using Duration to make sure that those affected burn for the next few rounds, I <i>must</i> have that gout of flame remain raging throughout the entire house?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're doing that, you're pretty much invariably using more Reach to add an Environmental Tilt to the effect, because otherwise you're just getting an AoE fireball that recurs once per casting interval.<br /> <br /> Spells that create areas of effect have persistent effects tied to that area. Spells that affect things that aren't themselves areas treat Area Scale like adding splash to the spell's effect, but don't cause extended Duration to make a persistent effect-field; Alter Direction works on anything coming into its area of effect because it's altering a quality within the area \u2014 the effect doesn't persist outside its bounds, which cannot be said for, say, turning every person in a small house into a frog without Dynamics (which is the difference between &quot;everyone in this house is a frog until the spell ends&quot; and &quot;anyone in this house is a frog until the spell ends.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-01-2017, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:01:09-08:00","id":1056510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056497#post1056497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're doing that, you're pretty much invariably using more Reach to add an Environmental Tilt to the effect, because otherwise you're just getting an AoE fireball that recurs once per casting interval.<br /> <br /> Spells that create areas of effect have persistent effects tied to that area. Spells that affect things that aren't themselves areas treat Area Scale like adding splash to the spell's effect, but don't cause extended Duration to make a persistent effect-field; Alter Direction works on anything coming into its area of effect because it's altering a quality within the area \u2014 the effect doesn't persist outside its bounds, which cannot be said for, say, turning every person in a small house into a frog without Dynamics (which is the difference between &quot;everyone in this house is a frog until the spell ends&quot; and &quot;anyone in this house is a frog until the spell ends.&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can add Tilts to a spell on purpose? I thought Tilts were just something extra that might happen if you're changing the environment straight up. I understand the difference of regular spells versus a Dynamic spell.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat's stupid is 2e mages have a lot in common with DnD 4e wizards. Controllers not Blasters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-01-2017, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:12:08-08:00","id":1056512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056510#post1056510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you can add Tilts to a spell on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Tilts are usually created by applying a Reach to an attack spell[.]&quot; Page 126, under Conditions and Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:14:15-08:00","id":1056514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056512#post1056512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Tilts are usually created by applying a Reach to an attack spell[.]&quot; Page 126, under Conditions and Tilts.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDamn...no other requirements? So any environmental/AOE/single target attack spell you can purposely add Tilts beyond the baseline? That could ridiculous if you have a rote for a spell that is inured..... it's why most Mages are Wisdom 4-5. What you actually think any mage getting off their ass is Wisdom 7+ or something more ridiculous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 03-01-2017, 03:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:16:30-08:00","id":1056624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056485#post1056485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sort of, there is only 1 mention of &quot;conjuctional&quot; in the entire book most spells now will now tell you what addition arcana you can add to do another effect and the conjuctional name has been dropped. There are also now attainments that can alter the way spells work, like sympathy and conditional duration, to exclude people from spells you now need to use a fate 2 spell called Warding Gesture.<br /> <br /> Ok, hmm, Say i cast a spell that turns everybody in an area into a frog. There is currently 3 people in the area. A,B and C, my spell works on A &amp; B but C has a higher withstand and so the spell faiils on them. A &amp; B are frogs, they will continue to be frogs until the spells duration ends even if they leave the area of effect right because my spell is making them a frog. Anybody else entering the area of effect will or wont be turned into a frog? I think that the spell will get cast agan every Gnosis limit if it also has a duration longer than instant and anybody in the area at that time will get turned into frogs? Thats how i see it working. If people do get turned into frogs by entering the area any time during its duration then C is still immune right (and i believe even if its withstand rating has changed) still its still the same spell?<br /> <br /> If you cast a aoe healing spell with a duration longer than instant, it will heal everybody in the area once and again every gnosis level? This is how i see every one time effect aoe spell working..<br /> <br /> Obv aoe spells that are creating/manipulating in their aoe will work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see this going one of two ways. Either it applies like damage or heal over time effects and hits everybody in the area with the spell effect once every ritual casting time increment <i><b>or</b></i> it applies continuously over the duration affecting <i>only </i>the people within its area and only for as long as they are in said area. It's a spell to turn everyone in the area into a frog, not specific people, so it would attempt to turn everyone who is in the area at the time of casting into frogs as well as anyone who entered before its duration was up, but anyone who left the area at any point would revert back to their previous form because the spell isn't targeting them specifically, so it won't follow them out as it were. <br /> <br /> I think my base assumption would be it functions continuously but the caster can probably make it function the other way at spell cast if they prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:40:04-08:00","id":1056633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056370#post1056370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure for spells with multiple targets, each target treats the spell as having its Potency lowered by their Withstand value. So, it might be reduced to 0 for one target, meaning it has no effect on them, but be only partially reduced for another target, still taking effect, but to a lesser degree than it would have if it was not Withstood. The question is, if said spell has a Duration longer than an instantaneous one-off effect, and one or more of the targets have their Withstand trait increased or decreased during that time, does the spell's Potency increase or decrease for that (or those) target (or targets) accordingly?<br /> <br /> For example, lets say I cast a spell on a group of five people that penalizes the target's attack dice pools by Potency for the Duration. Lets say that I set the Potency to 4 and the Duration to 1 scene. Lets say that this spell is Withstood by Composure. If in the five people affected, three have Composure 2 and two have Composure 3, two will have a -1 penalty to attack rolls for the Scenr and three will have a -2 penalty. If one of the people with Composure 3 somehow gains a dot of Composure during the scene, does it stop affecting him? If one of the people with Composure 2 loses a dot of Composure during the scene, does her penalty Increase to -3?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you are getting at here, but it seems to be just a restatement of the discussion. My point was that because the Potency of the Spell itself is separate per Target it is not 'eaten' as others said, just that its not strong enough to overcome the Withstand of a given Target. I was then extrapolating that becuase the spell still exists with full Potency it should take affect (or stop taking affect) on a target whose Withstand rating changes during it's Duration. Granted, that's an extraploation and not RAW.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T09:04:40-08:00","id":1056654,"title":"","content":"The problem with this interpretation is that it <i>flat-out doesn't work</i> for certain spells.<br /> <br /> Take degrading the form, for example. It's withstood by stamina, but it can also <i>affect </i>stamina. If withstand is a one-off effect that only applies when the spell is cast, this isn't a problem. But if the spell keeps it's initial potency and is withstood as an active effect then for spells like this the spell will erode the withstand attribute and then get more potency and erode the withstand attribute further, and get more potency...<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with the interpretation that doesn't <i>break the game</i>, if you don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T09:09:12-08:00","id":1056659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056654#post1056654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this interpretation is that it <i>flat-out doesn't work</i> for certain spells.<br /> <br /> Take degrading the form, for example. It's withstood by stamina, but it can also <i>affect </i>stamina. If withstand is a one-off effect that only applies when the spell is cast, this isn't a problem. But if the spell keeps it's initial potency and is withstood as an active effect then for spells like this the spell will erode the withstand attribute and then get more potency and erode the withstand attribute further, and get more potency...<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with the interpretation that doesn't <i>break the game</i>, if you don't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a pretty good point. I hadn't run into any spells that would have this problem. None of my current group have any dots in Life. Will think on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:04:09-08:00","id":1056671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056654#post1056654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this interpretation is that it <i>flat-out doesn't work</i> for certain spells.<br /> <br /> Take degrading the form, for example. It's withstood by stamina, but it can also <i>affect </i>stamina. If withstand is a one-off effect that only applies when the spell is cast, this isn't a problem. But if the spell keeps it's initial potency and is withstood as an active effect then for spells like this the spell will erode the withstand attribute and then get more potency and erode the withstand attribute further, and get more potency...<br /> <br /> I think I'll go with the interpretation that doesn't <i>break the game</i>, if you don't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that isn't how Potency works here at all. You choose when you cast the spell how much Potency said spell has, and that's all it is ever going to have. Lowering Withstand doesn't increase Potency. And even then Degrading the form only allows you to take an attribute down to 1, so it isn't some sort of infinite loop even if it did work the way you were thinking. At most you're getting your Potencys worth in stat reduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:15:45-08:00","id":1056675,"title":"","content":"Elfive never said it would be an infinite loop. The problem still persists with that interpretation since as long as you have Potency left after Withstand you'd reduce the Withstand trait to its minimum because of that loop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:16:46-08:00","id":1056677,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it would mean that since you need to beat someone's stamina by one to affect them there would a chain reaction that would knock them all the way down to one. And there's no way to prevent this.<br /> <br /> There's no real spell control here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:19:02-08:00","id":1056678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056675#post1056675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive never said it would be an infinite loop. The problem still persists with that interpretation since as long as you have Potency left after Withstand you'd reduce the Withstand trait to its minimum because of that loop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the person whose stats you're reducing has insane levels of stamina and you have an insane amount of potency it's functionally the same. And if you have enough dice to do that you'd be better off just aiming for an exceptional success and ignoring it completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:36:32-08:00","id":1056685,"title":"","content":"It means that if they have 4 stamina you need 5 potency instead of 7 to reduce them to one. That's four entire dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:02:26-08:00","id":1056715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056685#post1056685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means that if they have 4 stamina you need 5 potency instead of 7 to reduce them to one. That's four entire dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>For an eight-dice penalty, yes. And unless you've invested Reach in splitting the Potency toward multiple Attributes, that's <i>all</i> it'll do aside from weigh on your spell control while it's active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:35:17-08:00","id":1056736,"title":"","content":"It doesn't matter anyway. The fact that there's an obvious feedback loop tells me that that's not the writer's intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:46:00-08:00","id":1056742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056736#post1056736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter anyway. The fact that there's an obvious feedback loop tells me that that's not the writer's intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, here me out, or, we could just ask the writer what their intent was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:50:31-08:00","id":1056746,"title":"","content":"Well, sure. <br /> <br /> But I know what my money's on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:54:02-08:00","id":1056749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056746#post1056746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sure.<br /> <br /> But I know what my money's on.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see.<br /> <br /> Also, the feed back loop is probably to solve the issue of Stamina double dipping. The fact that you have to pay 2 potency for the lowering of every 1 point of Stamina you'd be going for. If you didn't, then to lower a Stamina of 5 to 1 you'd need to spend 8 potency, which equals out to 16 dice which is a bit crazy of a requirement just to mess with human levels of attributes.<br /> <br /> Fairly sure this was calculated and working as intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:00:45-08:00","id":1056754,"title":"","content":"The enemy supernaturals really only have to use their willpower to boost with withstand for 1 round because the Mage will likely be dead or dominated by the time that round is done, depending on the size of the group and what powers they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:16:30-08:00","id":1056761,"title":"","content":"Actually I think the fact that you can spend willpower to boost a withstand rating is the final nail in the coffin for the &quot;ongoing withstand&quot; argument. For the most part that would be <i>fucking useless</i>. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T13:34:01-08:00","id":1056773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056761#post1056761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think the fact that you can spend willpower to boost a withstand rating is the final nail in the coffin for the &quot;ongoing withstand&quot; argument. For the most part that would be <i>fucking useless</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It allows you to get out of area effect spells without getting hit by it, and allows you to resist spells with harsh, though short lasting effects. And since Willpower is specifically meant to be used often, it is an excuse to burn Willpower in order to continually resist the effects of a spell you wouldn't normally be able to for a time when it really matters (like, say, in combat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:03:23-08:00","id":1056790,"title":"","content":"I do believe we will need to hear from DaveB regarding this issue because it is definitely not clear either way and there are lots of questions regardless of what path you choose. Either the bookkeeping becomes a mess on one hand, or boosting Withstand temporarily quickly becomes useless for long duration spells.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we can receive some clarification, if only I knew what Supernal Being he happened to be I could find a Mage of the appropriate path to conjure him to these threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:09:33-08:00","id":1056793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taldorblackfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056790#post1056790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do believe we will need to hear from DaveB regarding this issue because it is definitely not clear either way and there are lots of questions regardless of what path you choose. Either the bookkeeping becomes a mess on one hand, or boosting Withstand temporarily quickly becomes useless for long duration spells.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we can receive some clarification, if only I knew what Supernal Being he happened to be I could find a Mage of the appropriate path to conjure him to these threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Group ritual cast with a member of every Path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T14:49:56-08:00","id":1056807,"title":"","content":"Withstand reduces the effect of a spell's Potency, it doesn't remove the spell. If someone's withstand rating changes part-way through a spell's Duration, up OR down, it gets reassessed. If your mind-control spell that isn't potent enough to beat someone's resolve is still active when something else reduces their resolve to below Potency, your mind control spell begins to work. Alternatively, if you mind control someone to kill themselves, they *can* spend Willpower at the last minute to up their Resolve for a turn. Or another mage can cast a spell that increases their Resolve, with a longer duration than your mind-control one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T15:20:48-08:00","id":1056814,"title":"","content":"How does it interact with ability to willingly not-Withstand spells? If an evil mage Mind Controls me and I actually have enough Resolve to poo on their spell, but want to spy on them, can I decide to not Withstand it now, but Withstand it later, being all GotV-Smug when I catch them redhanded? <br /> I like the idea that a lot of spells is quite similar to diseases; you are a host to potentially thousands of terrible stuff...but your organism is heroically withstanding them every day. And they wait for your defences to drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:09:42-08:00","id":1056830,"title":"","content":"Um, Dave, are you sure? This <i>totally breaks </i>Alter Integrity. It can increase an objects durability by potency, but is resisted by durability. So you increase the object's durability, which increases it's withstand rating by an equal amount.<br /> <br /> So the spell does nothing.<br /> <br /> Oh, it also breaks State Change, since transforming a gas or liquid gives the object durability equal to potency, and is also withstood by durability. So again, doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-01-2017, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:25:12-08:00","id":1056835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056830#post1056830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, Dave, are you sure? This <i>totally breaks </i>Alter Integrity. It can increase an objects durability by potency, but is resisted by durability. So you increase the object's durability, which increases it's withstand rating by an equal amount.<br /> <br /> So the spell does nothing.<br /> <br /> Oh, it also breaks State Change, since transforming a gas or liquid gives the object durability equal to potency, and is also withstood by durability. So again, doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, order of operations matters. Withstand is checked before the Spell takes affect (every time), so if you cast the Spell on a Durability 3 object with 4 Potency. The Spell changes its Durability to 4 (the difference in Potency is 1) and then it checks against the new Withstand rating and doesn't have the Potency to affect it anymore, so the object stays at Durability 4 for the Duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:31:22-08:00","id":1056839,"title":"","content":"...That's not how spells work. That would break about half the spells in the book, because a lot of them aren't withstood.<br /> <br /> Also what the hell happens if you give the gauntlet two strength ratings with Place of Power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-01-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:35:39-08:00","id":1056840,"title":"","content":"If it doesn't have the Potency to affect it anymore it would stop affecting it at all. As Dave said the spell should be reassessed after Withstand goes up meaning the spell has no Potency left and the effect is suppressed. And then it just continues to loop without a resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:41:34-08:00","id":1056844,"title":"","content":"Let's look at this example in practice:<br /> <br /> You have a Moros that is being chased down by a pack of zombies and he runs into a room. He quickly turns around and casts Alter Integrity on the door to grant it some more Durability, he places 4 Potency into the spell because he wants the door to hold them off while he thinks about his plan.<br /> <br /> Now, the Wooden Door has a durability of 1 normally, but this spell boosts that number to 5. Spell done, and the door failed to Withstand this increase in Durability. Let's say an Hour passes by and the spell was cast with 1 Day duration and the Moros has Gnosis 3. The spell stops affecting the door and again attempts the Withstand against the door, Durability 1 &lt; Potency 4, spell takes effect again.<br /> <br /> This is how the spell would work.<br /> <br /> Now, let's say another Moros stumbles across the door and decides, I best boost this door, he casts the same spell with Potency 4, but it is Withstood.... He goes, &quot;What?&quot; he analyzes the door and finds out it is reinforced already with another Matter Spell and moves on about his day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:44:10-08:00","id":1056845,"title":"","content":"Except Dave said that if the withstand rating changes the spell is <i>immediately</i> reassessed. Only spells with immediate effects like healing reoccur after gnosis intervals. Permanent effects are just... permanent.<br /> <br /> So the door is trapped in a superposition of having its durability boosted and not.<br /> <br /> So it may be a houserule now, but I think I'll stick with the interpretation that doesn't make my brain hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-01-2017, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:48:05-08:00","id":1056846,"title":"","content":"If the spell has 4 Potency and the door has 1 Durability the effect would have 3 effective Potency and increase Durability to 4, but immediately the Withstand rating has been increased and the spell has no effect at all. But that means the Withstand rating has decreased so the spell takes effect. But then the Withstand rating has increased again and the spell stops being effective. Et cetera.<br /> <br /> Here's a quick house rule that solves both increasing and decreasing Withstand: Whenever a spell would alter a Withstand rating that affects the spell, the spell is Withstood by the higher of those ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:49:24-08:00","id":1056848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056807#post1056807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alternatively, if you mind control someone to kill themselves, they *can* spend Willpower at the last minute to up their Resolve for a turn. Or another mage can cast a spell that increases their Resolve, with a longer duration than your mind-control one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Personally i wouldn't allow it. Since your not doing what you have been controlled to do. What if your told to kill yourself and not to resist?<br /> Cos i know the first time i told somebody to kill themselves and they were about to do it but then resisted i'd tell them not to resist it the next time..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:53:25-08:00","id":1056851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056846#post1056846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a quick house rule that solves both increasing and decreasing Withstand: Whenever a spell would alter a Withstand rating that affects the spell, the spell is Withstood by the higher of those ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't solve the increasing problem at all. It just makes it definitely not work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T16:54:08-08:00","id":1056853,"title":"","content":"Hey, look at that. The developer stated his intent and no one's mind was changed by it.<br /> <br /> In other news, recent study suggests there may be a correlation between hydrogen dioxide and moisture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:06:26-08:00","id":1056860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1055378-mage-is-biting-us-in-the-ass-every-step-of-the-way?p=1056851#post1056851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't solve the increasing problem at all. It just makes it definitely not work.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spells that reduce their own mitigating factors don't benefit from that selfsame reduction&quot; doesn't seem like a non-solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-